    <!--
      Short stillness prompts. All original wording, one plain idea each, anchored
      in sound, breath, touch, and body sensation. No copyrighted quotes are
      bundled. People can add their own lines, including quotes they love, in the
      "Your prompts" section.
    -->
    <string-array name="stillness_prompts">
        <item>Notice your feet on the floor.</item>
        <item>Feel the weight of your hands where they rest.</item>
        <item>Listen for the furthest sound you can hear.</item>
        <item>Notice the temperature of the air on your skin.</item>
        <item>Let your shoulders drop a little.</item>
        <item>Feel your breath at the tip of your nose.</item>
        <item>Notice where your body meets the chair or bed.</item>
        <item>Unclench your jaw, and let it be soft.</item>
        <item>Feel the air move in, and then out.</item>
        <item>Rest your attention on one small sound nearby.</item>
        <item>Notice the gentle rise and fall of your chest.</item>
        <item>Let this breath be a little slower than the last.</item>
        <item>Feel the ground holding you up.</item>
        <item>Soften the space between your eyebrows.</item>
        <item>Notice one thing you can hear, and let it be enough.</item>
        <item>Let your hands be still and open.</item>
        <item>Feel the warmth of your own breath.</item>
        <item>Notice the pause at the end of the out breath.</item>
        <item>Let your tongue rest soft in your mouth.</item>
        <item>Come back to this breath, just this one.</item>
        <item>Notice the weight of your body settling down.</item>
        <item>Let the next breath arrive on its own.</item>
        <item>Feel the small movements of sitting still.</item>
        <item>Rest here for a moment, nothing to fix.</item>
        <item>Notice the quiet underneath the sounds.</item>
    </string-array>
